  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and actuation: perception states reflect obstacle sensors, and actuation states reflect motion commands. The specification binds sensor outcomes to safe, coverage-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when needed and maximizing exploration via random_walk and short forward pulses. Recovery from obstacles is handled with directed turns or, as a last resort, a full scan. The supervisor always returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion, with all events atomic and deterministic.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward in commit, directed turn recovery on obstacles, and full_rotate only after repeated blockages."
